# ── Environment / Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# ── ARTA runtime state + secrets under .arta/ — DEFAULT-DENY ───────────────────
# Everything under the top-level `.arta/` runtime dir is ignored unless
# explicitly re-included below. The previous allow-by-default list went stale
# every time the pipeline grew a new runtime dir (architecture_discovery/,
# audit/, regen_queue/, runs/, traceability/, improvement_loop/, root_cause/,
# upstream_quality/, github_cache/, discovered_response_shapes/,
# frontend_routes/, ...) and let thousands of per-run files AND live secrets
# (storage-state session cookies, operator-pasted JWTs, R98.1-synced Postman
# auth_token values, projects.json integration tokens) slip into the index.
# Fail-closed: a new runtime dir or secrets file is ignored without anyone
# having to remember to add a pattern.
#
# The pattern is LEADING-SLASH ANCHORED to repo root so it only matches the
# top-level `.arta/` runtime dir (NOT `src/.arta/` test fixtures, etc.).
/.arta/*

# Re-include the files that ARE source. Operator copies *.example.json to the
# active path; the API auto-creates runtime dirs on first write, so no
# `.gitkeep` is needed inside ignored dirs.
!/.arta/arta.config.yaml
!/.arta/projects.example.json

# Committed Gherkin scenarios (e.g. bugtrackr/) are operator-curated source.
# Auto-generated scenarios land here too — prune at curation time if unwanted.
!/.arta/scenarios/

# environments/ mixes tracked config templates with live secrets, so it gets
# its own inner default-deny: re-include the dir, ignore its children, then
# re-include ONLY the secret-free templates. Storage-state files (live session
# cookies pasted via the R15 Refresh Auth modal), their .bak / .meta.json
# siblings, and Newman envs carrying a real auth_token JWT (e.g.
# token — use {{PLACEHOLDER}} values like staging.json does.
!/.arta/environments/
/.arta/environments/*
!/.arta/environments/staging.json
!/.arta/environments/bugtrackr-local.json

# ── Generated / quarantined test artifacts (LLM-emitted, may be regenerated) ──
# `tools/regen_existing_tests.py` quarantines failed regenerations as
# `.broken-<reason>` siblings; the original is renamed to `.pre-N.bak`.
# Both are debugging aids on the operator's machine, not source.
*.broken
*.broken-*
*.pre-N.bak
*.pre-*.bak

